  <section class="lab-section first">
    <h1>About Txchyon</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A small lab that researches crypto trading strategies and builds the software to test them. Nothing here is for sale.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="lab-section tight prose">
    <h2>What we do</h2>
    <p>
      We test trading ideas on real market data, keep notes on what works and what doesn't, and build apps and learning tools along the
      way. Wins and losses both get written down.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Software.</b> The Txchyon app is a rules-based spot trading bot with a phone app to watch and control it. It runs on paper first. See <a href="/#software">the app</a>.</li>
      <li><b>Lab notes.</b> Short, honest updates on backtests and paper results. See <a href="/#notes">lab notes</a>.</li>
      <li><b>The blog.</b> Guides on crypto basics, security, DeFi, airdrops and tax. See the <a href="/blog">blog</a>.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who</h2>
    <p>
      Txchyon is built by <a href="https://x.com/expatbuilder" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ExpatBuildr</a>
      (<a href="https://github.com/ExpatBuildr" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>). Follow the project on
      <a href="https://x.com/txchyon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">X</a> and
      <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@Txchyon" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouTube</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site is not</h2>
    <p>
      It is research and software, not investment advice. We don't give signals or manage money. Some older articles contain affiliate
      links; see the <a href="/disclaimer">disclaimer</a> and the <a href="/tools">tools page</a>.
    </p>

    <p><a class="btn" href="/contact">Get in touch</a></p>
  </section>
